  "definition": "Drosophila here refers to Drosophila melanogaster, the organism used as an experimental model to examine how a high-sucrose diet affects physiology, biochemistry, behavior, and gene activity. In this context, it is a research model for studying diet-related changes relevant to metabolic disorders.",
